   "text": "Deadline is the EARLIER of (a) the sixth business day strictly after today and (b) the last business day of the current calendar month; neither boundary may be exceeded. The DSL has no min-of-two rule, so the deadline is encoded as nth_business_day n=6 with an extra 'cap' (end_of_month, business basis, current month) and combine='earlier'; the compiler must apply the cap.",
   "doc": "tests/fixtures/external/codex-cedar-limits/01-specification.md"
